{"seq":28,"slug":"scala-language","title":"Scala 语言","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language","rating":{"composite":3.86,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# Scala 语言\n\nScala 把两种长期被认为对立的编程范式焊在了同一门语言里：源自 Java 世界的面向对象建模，与源自 ML/Haskell 世界的函数式抽象。它不是在 JVM 上「再造一个 Java」，而是把类、特质与不可变值、高阶函数放进同一套静态类型系统中，让二者互相成全。理解 Scala，本质上是理解这种融合如何在类型层面被精确地表达出来。\n\n本 hub 按「基础 → 函数式 → 类型系统 → 生态」四章层层递进，每一章都建立在前一章的概念之上，不重复展开同一主题。\n\n第一章「基础」铺设地基：Scala 在 JVM 生态中的定位与版本现状、面向对象与函数式如何在 trait 与 case class 上交汇、以及让这一切写起来不啰嗦的局部类型推断。读完这一章，你能读懂大部分 Scala 代码的形状。\n\n第二章「函数式」进入 Scala 的灵魂：默认不可变的集合库与持久化数据结构、作为一等控制流的模式匹配、以及把高阶函数、for 推导与 Monad 抽象串成一条线的组合哲学。这一章解释「为什么 Scala 程序读起来像数据在流动」。\n\n第三章「类型系统」是 Scala 区别于多数主流语言的硬核所在：型变、路径依赖类型、opaque type、联合与交集类型等高级构造；given/using 这套上下文抽象机制；以及在它之上自然生长出来的类型类模式。这一章解释「为什么 Scala 能把约束写进类型，让编译器替你检查」。\n\n第四章「生态」把前三章的能力落到工程现场：基于纯函数描述并发与副作用的效应系统（Future、Cats Effect、ZIO）、Scala 3 带来的语法与元编程革新、以及 Spark、sbt、scala-cli、Metals 构成的真实工具链与大数据应用。这一章是收口，回答「学完这些能干什么」。\n\n四条主线——OO/FP 融合、不可变与组合、类型即契约、效应即值——贯穿全 hub。建议顺序阅读：每篇文档只深讲属于自己的概念，遇到别处主讲的主题会用一句话点到并交叉链接过去，让你在需要时跳转，而不必在多处重读同一内容。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"scala-overview","title":"Scala 概览与定位","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/foundations/scala-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"oop-fp-fusion","title":"面向对象与函数式融合","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/foundations/oop-fp-fusion"},{"seq":3,"slug":"type-inference-basics","title":"类型推断基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/foundations/type-inference-basics"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"functional","title":"函数式","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/functional","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"immutability-collections","title":"不可变与集合","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/functional/immutability-collections"},{"seq":2,"slug":"pattern-matching","title":"模式匹配","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/functional/pattern-matching"},{"seq":3,"slug":"higher-order-monads","title":"高阶函数与 Monad","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/functional/higher-order-monads"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"type-system","title":"类型系统","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/type-system","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"advanced-types","title":"高级类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/type-system/advanced-types"},{"seq":2,"slug":"implicits-givens","title":"隐式与 given","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/type-system/implicits-givens"},{"seq":3,"slug":"type-classes","title":"类型类","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/type-system/type-classes"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"ecosystem","title":"生态","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/ecosystem","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"concurrency-effects","title":"并发与效应系统","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/ecosystem/concurrency-effects"},{"seq":2,"slug":"scala3-features","title":"Scala 3 特性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/ecosystem/scala3-features"},{"seq":3,"slug":"spark-tooling","title":"Spark 与工具链","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/scala-language/ecosystem/spark-tooling"}]}]}